# COMMITTED BUT DORMANT. A timer only fires after an administrator installs it and runs `systemctl enable --now donchian-forward-collection.timer`; merely
# being in this directory (or in the mechanism image) does nothing. The wrapper it triggers also refuses without its arming file.
#
# Two fires per session day, both on the calendar day AFTER the session, in Jerusalem time (the tag every other production timer uses):
#   06:45  first attempt. It follows the night's single price-discontinuity scan (donchian-discontinuity-scan.timer, 06:20), which itself follows the final
#          post-market retry (06:00 start, 9-16 min). That retry loads the late-arriving bars (a recurring straggler arrived 23:46Z-02:47Z on four consecutive
#          nights), so by 06:45 the stored prices, the scan evidence and the pipeline's output are final for the night. The collector is still NOT trusted to
#          mean "everything is done": it verifies the session's own price bar, a COMPLETE scan whose fingerprints match the stored prices, the sector-history
#          polls and (once capture is enabled) a COMPLETE capture run; anything missing yields INCOMPLETE (exit 2, an alert state), never COMPLETE.
#   08:15  the recovery attempt: the same session again. It cannot repair a stale scan (strict fingerprint rule), but a session whose snapshot is already
#          committed and valid is REUSED read-only (never rewritten, never turned INCOMPLETE by a later price change), so the second fire is an idempotent check.
# The second fire's worst case (08:15 + 45 min timeout + 60 s) is still before 00:00 UTC of session+2, so with availability_grace_days=1 every
# observation this schedule can write is known before its decision deadline (contract.required_grace_days() computes this over every weekday of
# both daylight-saving offsets; a test pins it). The weekend fires find nothing new to do and exit 0 ("latest completed session" is unchanged).
[Timer]
OnCalendar=*-*-* 06:45:00 Asia/Jerusalem
OnCalendar=*-*-* 08:15:00 Asia/Jerusalem
Persistent=true
RandomizedDelaySec=60

[Install]
WantedBy=timers.target
